<!-- [XPLAT] migrated from net48/WinForms — see MIGRATION_DOCS/TRANSITION_MAP.md -->
<!--
    [XPLAT] AgOpenGPS (GPS program) — "2 Points - Align Grid" dialog (Avalonia view).

    1:1 visual + behavioural PARITY reimplementation of the WinForms
    Forms/Guidance/FormGrid (source: FormGrid.cs + FormGrid.Designer.cs). Per AAP §0.3.3 this
    is a faithful re-platform of the currently rendered Windows Forms surface, never a redesign:
    every size, position, colour and font below is taken verbatim from FormGrid.Designer.cs
    (WinForms pixels map 1:1 to Avalonia device-independent pixels at 96 dpi; point font sizes
    are converted pt x 96/72 -> DIP).

    The dialog shows the field in a square OpenGL viewport. The operator taps two points in the
    viewport to define a direction (point A then point B) and the world-grid is rotated to that
    AB heading; alternatively "Align to track" snaps the grid to the active guidance track. The
    four buttons down the right edge clear the tapped points, align to track, cancel (reset the
    grid rotation to 0), or accept and close.

    CODE-BEHIND CONTRACT — FormGridView.axaml.cs (partial class AgOpenGPS.Views.FormGridView : Window):
      * This view is IMPERATIVE, not MVVM: there is intentionally NO x:DataType, no DataContext
        and no {Binding}. The x:Name'd controls below are the entire integration surface and keep
        their ORIGINAL WinForms names so the migrated code-behind addresses them exactly as
        FormGrid.cs / FormGrid.Designer.cs did. No handlers are wired in this markup — the
        code-behind attaches them by name (reproducing the WinForms handlers):
          - ViewportHost   : the Black square Border that hosts the injected GL surface. The
                             code-behind sets ViewportHost.Child = viewport.View (the companion
                             control of AgOpenGPS.Controls.AvaloniaGeoViewport — the cross-platform
                             replacement for the WinForms OpenTK.GLControl "oglSelf"), attaches the
                             PointerPressed tap handler to it (was oglSelf_MouseDown — captures the
                             two GeoCoords and rotates worldGrid), and keeps it square on resize
                             (was FormABDraw_ResizeEnd: oglSelf is sized Height-40 and the button
                             column re-anchored to its right).
          - btnCancelTouch : clears the two tapped points and resets zoom/pan (was btnCancelTouch_Click).
          - btnAlignToTrack: rotates the world-grid to the active track's AB heading and closes
                             (was btnAlignToTrack_Click).
          - btnCancel      : resets worldGrid.gridRotation to 0 and closes (was btnCancel_Click).
          - btnExit        : accepts and closes (was btnExit_Click).

    WINDOW SHELL — mirrors FormGrid.Designer.cs:
      Text "2 Points - Align Grid" -> Title (design-time literal; the source assigns this.Text
                                      directly — no gStr key is used for this caption).
      ClientSize 605 x 501         -> Width / Height 605 x 501 (the source ClientSize; where native
                                      decorations are drawn outside the client the title bar takes a
                                      few pixels — a documented minor deviation, mitigated by
                                      CanResize="True").
      BackColor WhiteSmoke         -> Background {DynamicResource AogLegacyWhiteSmokeBrush}. This
                                      App.axaml token IS Color.WhiteSmoke (#FFF5F5F5); it is used
                                      instead of the raw literal so the Views layer references one
                                      named, self-documenting parity resource (App.axaml rationale).
                                      The dialog is a FIXED light surface — it was never part of the
                                      FormGPS day/night SwapDayNightMode chrome — so it is NOT bound
                                      to the day/night AogFrameBrush.
      ControlBox = false,          -> [XPLAT] Avalonia cannot hide only the caption buttons; the
      HelpButton = true,              no-control-box / help-button look is approximated by keeping
      Max/MinimizeBox = false         the normal title bar (SystemDecorations="Full"). The dialog is
                                      driven by its own Cancel / OK buttons exactly as the source.
      ShowInTaskbar = false        -> ShowInTaskbar="False".
      StartPosition CenterParent   -> WindowStartupLocation="Manual": the code-behind restores the
                                      persisted setWindow_gridLocation/Size (was FormABDraw_Load),
                                      falling back to CenterOwner when no valid location is stored.
      ResizeEnd persists size      -> CanResize="True" (the source persists setWindow_gridSize and
                                      re-runs the square/anchor layout in FormABDraw_ResizeEnd).

    Button glyphs are served from the GPS assembly (assembly name "AgOpenGPS") via avares:// URIs,
    mapped from the Designer's Image assignments (assets live under btnImages\, included as
    <AvaloniaResource> in AgOpenGPS.csproj):
      btnCancelTouch.Image  = Resources.HeadlandDeletePoints -> btnImages/HeadlandDeletePoints.png
      btnAlignToTrack.Image = Resources.ABTrackAB            -> btnImages/ABTrackAB.png
      btnCancel.Image       = Resources.Cancel64             -> btnImages/Cancel64.png
      btnExit.Image         = Resources.OK64                 -> btnImages/OK64.png

    No System.Windows.Forms, no OpenTK.GLControl, no GMap, no ColorPicker types are referenced —
    Avalonia 11.3 markup only.
-->
<Window xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
        xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
        x:Class="AgOpenGPS.Views.FormGridView"
        Title="2 Points - Align Grid"
        Width="605"
        Height="501"
        Background="{DynamicResource AogLegacyWhiteSmokeBrush}"
        SystemDecorations="Full"
        CanResize="True"
        ShowInTaskbar="False"
        WindowStartupLocation="Manual">

    <!--
        Flat, chrome-less push buttons reproduce the WinForms FlatStyle.Flat +
        FlatAppearance.BorderSize = 0 + BackColor.Transparent face: just the scaled glyph, with no
        button surface in any interaction state. The :pointerover / :pressed template overrides
        suppress the Fluent hover/press fill that would otherwise box the glyph (the proven sibling
        convention — see Guidance/FormSmoothABView, FormYesView, FormPanView). FormGrid uses only
        Buttons (no RepeatButton), so a single Button.flatImage style class is declared.
    -->
    <Window.Styles>
        <Style Selector="Button.flatImage">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="0" />
            <Setter Property="Padding" Value="0" />
            <Setter Property="HorizontalContentAlignment" Value="Center" />
            <Setter Property="VerticalContentAlignment" Value="Center" />
        </Style>
        <Style Selector="Button.flatImage:pointerover /template/ ContentPresenter#PART_ContentPresenter">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="Transparent" />
        </Style>
        <Style Selector="Button.flatImage:pressed /template/ ContentPresenter#PART_ContentPresenter">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="Transparent" />
        </Style>
    </Window.Styles>

    <!--
        Root layout == the WinForms client area split into two regions, mirroring the Designer's
        oglSelf (left) + tlp1 (right): a flexible left column holding the square viewport host, and
        an auto-width right column holding the vertical button strip. The code-behind keeps the
        viewport square on resize (FormABDraw_ResizeEnd) and re-anchors the strip to its right edge.
    -->
    <Grid>
        <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
            <ColumnDefinition Width="*" />
            <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto" />
        </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>

        <!-- oglSelf -> ViewportHost: WinForms OpenTK.GLControl @ (2,2), BackColor Black, Cursor
             Cross, 500 x 500, kept square (Height-40) by the resize handler. In Avalonia the GL
             surface is the injected AgOpenGPS.Controls.AvaloniaGeoViewport; the code-behind sets
             this Border's Child to viewport.View and attaches the PointerPressed tap handler. The
             Black background shows through until the GL surface paints, exactly like the WinForms
             control's BackColor. Margin 2 reproduces the (2,2) inset. -->
        <Border x:Name="ViewportHost"
                Grid.Column="0"
                Background="Black"
                Margin="2"
                Cursor="Cross" />

        <!-- tlp1: WinForms TableLayoutPanel anchored Top|Bottom|Right, 1 column x 4 rows, ~99 wide.
             Reproduced as a single-column 4-row Grid so the four buttons distribute down the full
             height (btnExit pinned to the bottom row) and stay distributed as the window resizes —
             the responsive equivalent of the TableLayoutPanel row styles (~20%/20%/20% + a taller
             bottom row). Each button is centred in its row (the WinForms Anchor.None). x:Name kept
             as "tlp1" for the code-behind's resize/anchor math. -->
        <Grid x:Name="tlp1"
              Grid.Column="1"
              Width="99">
            <Grid.RowDefinitions>
                <RowDefinition Height="*" />
                <RowDefinition Height="*" />
                <RowDefinition Height="*" />
                <RowDefinition Height="*" />
            </Grid.RowDefinitions>

            <!-- btnCancelTouch: WinForms Button row 0, 54 x 56, Image HeadlandDeletePoints,
                 FlatStyle.Flat + BorderSize 0 + BackColor Transparent + BackgroundImageLayout Zoom.
                 Clears the two tapped points and resets zoom/pan (btnCancelTouch_Click). The glyph
                 scales uniformly to fit the 54 x 56 face (the Zoom parity). -->
            <Button x:Name="btnCancelTouch"
                    Grid.Row="0"
                    Classes="flatImage"
                    Width="54" Height="56"
                    HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                    AutomationProperties.Name="Clear touch points">
                <Image Source="avares://AgOpenGPS/btnImages/HeadlandDeletePoints.png"
                       Width="54" Height="56" Stretch="Uniform" />
            </Button>

            <!-- btnAlignToTrack: WinForms Button row 1, 54 x 81, Image ABTrackAB, FlatStyle.Flat +
                 BorderSize 0 + BackColor Transparent + Zoom. Rotates the world-grid to the active
                 track's AB heading and closes (btnAlignToTrack_Click). -->
            <Button x:Name="btnAlignToTrack"
                    Grid.Row="1"
                    Classes="flatImage"
                    Width="54" Height="81"
                    HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                    AutomationProperties.Name="Align grid to track">
                <Image Source="avares://AgOpenGPS/btnImages/ABTrackAB.png"
                       Width="54" Height="81" Stretch="Uniform" />
            </Button>

            <!-- btnCancel: WinForms Button row 2, 54 x 56, Image Cancel64, FlatStyle.Flat +
                 BorderSize 0 + BackColor Transparent + Zoom (DialogResult.Cancel). Resets
                 worldGrid.gridRotation to 0 and closes (btnCancel_Click). -->
            <Button x:Name="btnCancel"
                    Grid.Row="2"
                    Classes="flatImage"
                    Width="54" Height="56"
                    HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                    AutomationProperties.Name="Cancel">
                <Image Source="avares://AgOpenGPS/btnImages/Cancel64.png"
                       Width="54" Height="56" Stretch="Uniform" />
            </Button>

            <!-- btnExit: WinForms Button row 3, 54 x 56, Image OK64, FlatStyle.Flat + BorderSize 0 +
                 BackColor Transparent. Font Tahoma 15.75pt Bold (-> 21 DIP) and ForeColor
                 Color.FromArgb(192,64,0) (#FFC04000) are carried verbatim for exact parity even
                 though the source assigns no .Text to this button (the font/colour are therefore
                 inert with the image-only content, but reproduce the Designer exactly and apply if
                 the code-behind ever sets a caption). Accepts and closes (btnExit_Click). -->
            <Button x:Name="btnExit"
                    Grid.Row="3"
                    Classes="flatImage"
                    Width="54" Height="56"
                    HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                    FontFamily="Tahoma"
                    FontSize="21"
                    FontWeight="Bold"
                    Foreground="#FFC04000"
                    AutomationProperties.Name="Accept">
                <Image Source="avares://AgOpenGPS/btnImages/OK64.png"
                       Width="54" Height="56" Stretch="Uniform" />
            </Button>

        </Grid>
    </Grid>
</Window>
